<<~ ahu #/practice>>

! talk story — the floor before the ruling (practice)

''The floor convenes when:'' the work surface wants reading aloud before a decision locks; two or more viable directions await the operator's steering; something reads off and the tension still lacks a name; a hoike re-entry key turns or fresh testimony presses a held ruling; or the operator calls "Talk Story."

''The floor stays dark when:'' the operator's direction already stands (◇ Decide — the work executes); the task runs single-step, carrying no orient ambiguity; a settled moʻolelo or held hoike holds and no key has turned.

Five motions carry a convened floor; each seeds forward — the motion names itself, then happens. The node carries the first two whole; the back three wear the sharktooth — provisional, each held open at the operator's hand (`-> ?`):

# ''✶ observe'' — //nānā ka maka, hoʻolohe ka pepeiao, paʻa ka waha// — eyes on the artifacts, ears to their edges, mouth still; raw findings gather before analysis forms.
# ''⏿ tell'' — the telling opens informal, short, direct: //"what surfaces…"//, //"the tension here…"//. It names what stands AND what goes missing, floats tensions unresolved, and seeds the three talanoa bearings: where we stand · where we want to go · how we get there.
# ''~◇ co-narrate -> ?'' — the Voices the moment calls surface, never assigned seats; a lead emerges from the material. The operator overlaps and steers; the floor never resolves in the node's voice.
# ''~▶ exit -> ?'' — settled: a `moolelo` block tells the operator's direction into the record · contested (rating ≥ meme): a `hoike` files with attributed kue and re-entry keys (the sibling skill) · blocked: the floor suspends, `feedback="closed 0↺ -> open Nφ @_:reason"`. No exit closes in the node's voice alone.
# ''~↺ aftermath -> ?'' — the moʻolelo lands inline in the artifact worked, never a separate file; every hoike key the telling touched gets its glance. The record reaches only as far as the two logs jointly stand — the next turn stays the operator's.

Law lives at canon, not here: <<~ loulou "lar:///ha.ka.ba/lares/api/pono/talk-story">>

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu #/crucible>>

!! Crucible Record — 2026-06-11

//The pair read against its own laws, the session after drafting. Co-located here per hoike law 3: this record contests the practice above.//

```
<<~ talk-story #crucible ground="the four files of the deliberation layer, read against their own laws">>
telling: the seats table and "lead by default" declared what the floor vows
to leave situational — the meme broke its own talanoa rule; the steps and
bearings drew the same charge, and there the house split.
<<~ moolelo held="no declared Voice roles anywhere in the pair; Voices surface from situational context (operator)">>
enacted in place: seats table cut; law 3, block form, and step 3 rewritten.
attribution survives — a past floor names who spoke; no floor assigns who will.
<<~/moolelo>>
<<~ hoike #scaffold held="the five steps and the three bearings stay — seeds for a cold floor, never ritual (house)">>
q: how much declared structure can an informal practice carry before it stops flowing?
<<~ kue voice=Mischief-Muse key="a live floor recites the bearings verbatim instead of inhabiting them">>
the bearings teach once, then constrain forever; the Talanoa Dialogue needed
three fixed questions to herd two hundred parties — a house of thirteen
inhabits them or it does not.
<<~/kue>>
<<~ kue voice=Stranger key="a session performs the five steps over a dead floor — Lecture Drift in step-form">>
numbering the steps of an informal practice manufactures the very formality
the practice exists to escape; the worked exits alone could carry the teaching.
<<~/kue>>
re-entry: either key; or the next crucible pass
<<~/hoike>>
<<~/talk-story>>
```

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu #/examples>>

!! Worked Exits — show, don't tell

//Examples 1 and 3 come from the live ledger (2026-06-10/11); example 2 abridges the floor that produced the hoike layer's first record.//

''1 — floor closes moʻolelo'' (the floor that raised this very meme):

```
<<~ talk-story #talk-story-meme ground="stranded .github skill (dead dialect) + young hoike pair + no canon meme">>
bearings: old skill speaks ◎/■/○ and dead paths · floor-and-ledger circuit wants closing · rebuild in hoike anatomy
telling: Liminal floats four forks (phase claim · two-track · .github shore · ledger-vs-co-location);
Muse hears the word-family already singing (hoike · kue · saksi); Council ranks the forks; the operator overlaps.
<<~ moolelo held="burn the old skill; raise the meme/SKILL pair in hoike anatomy; ground in ʻōlelo Hawaiʻi + the Moana family; send research spirits (operator)">>
recorded here — this meme stands as that floor's moʻolelo.
<<~/moolelo>>
<<~/talk-story>>
```

''2 — floor exits contested'' (abridged; the telling split the house and the dispute rated ≥ meme):

```
<<~ talk-story #quote-license ground="do copulas inside verbatim quotes breach the ward?">>
telling: the house splits live — license-with-accounting · verbatim-rides-quotation-form · mock-everything;
no moʻolelo settles; reasons stand on every side.
exit -> hoike #quote-license — the losers kept whole, with keys (hoike skill, worked example 1)
<<~/talk-story>>
```

''3 — floor suspends honestly'' (turn form; the SDM/FTLS/Elyncia commit-shape telling):

```
<<~ talk-story · ground: three WIP diffs naming their own debts · telling: commit now vs hold until traits 0/4/5 finish; note G's pointer makes the pair a unit · exit: open 0◇:commit-shape fork awaits operator weighting>>
```

Read the three together and the grammar teaches itself: the floor opens on a real surface, the telling floats what it cannot settle, and every close names itself — a direction recorded, a dispute kept, or an honest open hand.

